---
// History.astro - Merged background tab: condensed work history + org pills
// + Meds/Labs reduced to TL;DR strips. Full record lives in the resume PDF.

const timelineCards = [
  {
    title: 'Clinical workflow and documentation systems',
    intro: 'Most recent clinical work: remote triage, chronic care, and documentation-heavy healthcare operations.',
    items: [
      'Mapped nurse-led triage and care-management workflows into clearer decision lanes',
      'Designed structured documentation components that reduced repeated entry and improved consistency',
      'Worked directly inside EHR and remote-care systems where the practical question is whether a tool supports safe work',
    ],
  },
  {
    title: 'Emergency, rehab, and high-acuity environments',
    intro: 'Earlier acute and post-acute work shaped how I think about handoffs, failure modes, and cognitive load.',
    items: [
      'Worked where unclear lanes, incomplete information, and timing pressure directly affect safety',
      'Learned to treat handoff quality, escalation logic, and documentation clarity as operational safety issues, not administrative preferences',
    ],
  },
  {
    title: 'Technical and governed AI systems',
    intro: 'In parallel with nursing: software that supports judgment without becoming unaccountable infrastructure.',
    items: [
      'Built local-first tools for document intake, knowledge organization, operational memory, and review workflows',
      'Designed governance patterns for human-reviewed AI output, audit trails, state visibility, and boundary enforcement',
      'Python, JavaScript/TypeScript, SQL, FastAPI, React, SQLite, Pytest, Playwright, and REST APIs across applied prototypes',
    ],
  },
  {
    title: 'Experimental and creative systems',
    intro: 'Work outside traditional software categories that informs how I think about resilience, feedback, and constraints.',
    items: [
      'Built and tested small biological systems: hydroponics, aquaponics, nutrient-flow experiments, regenerative garden layouts',
      'Developed ecommerce and creative infrastructure; photography and macro videography as studies in signal and attention',
    ],
  },
];

const clinicalOrgs = [
  'Signallamp Health / Tellihealth',
  'Nobis Health / Orlando Rehabilitation Hospital',
  'Encompass Health',
  'VitaLounge',
  'Quantum Health',
  'Southeastern Ohio Regional Medical Center',
  'Grant Medical Center (OhioHealth)',
  'Nationwide Children’s Hospital',
  'Grant Life Link',
  'MedCorp EMS',
];

const creativeOrgs = [
  'Independent software prototypes',
  'Visual media and ecommerce systems',
  'Local-first knowledge and workflow tools',
  'Biological and garden-system experiments',
];

const medsPills = [
  'Map the real workflow',
  'Clarify the lanes',
  'Structure the documentation',
  'Preserve human judgment',
  'Automate only what can be evaluated',
];

const labsPills = [
  'Friction & rework',
  'Handoff quality',
  'Cognitive load',
  'Provenance & review status',
  'Behavior under stress',
];
---

<div class="tab-panel" id="panel-history">
  <h2>History - Systems I Have Worked Inside</h2>

  <p class="tldr"><strong>TL;DR:</strong> Clinical triage, emergency care, rehab operations, EHR documentation, local-first software, governed AI, biological systems, ecommerce infrastructure.</p>

  <p>My work is systems-first because my background has been systems-heavy. I have worked inside clinical environments where unclear handoffs create risk, remote workflows where documentation becomes infrastructure, and technical projects where a system is only useful if it behaves safely under constraint.</p>

  <div class="timeline-cards">
    {timelineCards.map((card) => (
      <section class="card">
        <h3>{card.title}</h3>
        <p class="card-intro">{card.intro}</p>
        <ul>
          {card.items.map((item) => (
            <li>{item}</li>
          ))}
        </ul>
      </section>
    ))}
  </div>

  <h3>Organizations and contexts</h3>
  <p class="card-intro">A non-exhaustive list of organizations whose systems and workflows have shaped how I think.</p>
  <div class="pill-strip" aria-label="Healthcare and clinical organizations">
    {clinicalOrgs.map((org) => (
      <span class="pill">{org}</span>
    ))}
  </div>
  <div class="pill-strip" aria-label="Creative and systems-adjacent contexts">
    {creativeOrgs.map((org) => (
      <span class="pill secondary">{org}</span>
    ))}
  </div>

  <h3>Meds – Interventions I Reach For</h3>
  <div class="pill-strip" aria-label="Standing orders">
    {medsPills.map((item) => (
      <span class="pill">{item}</span>
    ))}
  </div>
  <p class="strip-note">I do not treat AI as the intervention by default. Often the useful intervention is upstream: naming the workflow, reducing ambiguity, strengthening documentation, and deciding where automation is safe enough to test.</p>

  <h3>Labs – Signals I Watch</h3>
  <div class="pill-strip" aria-label="Signal panel">
    {labsPills.map((item) => (
      <span class="pill">{item}</span>
    ))}
  </div>
  <p class="strip-note">A system can look successful while quietly transferring burden to the people inside it. These are the signals I watch before trusting the story the dashboard tells.</p>

  <p class="full-record">
    This is the condensed chart. The full record lives in
    <a href="/assets/resume.pdf" download>the resume (PDF)</a>.
  </p>
</div>

<style>
  .tldr {
    background: var(--bg-secondary);
    padding: 1rem;
    border-left: 3px solid var(--color-teal);
    margin: 1.5rem 0;
    font-size: 0.95rem;
  }

  #panel-history h3 {
    color: var(--color-teal);
    margin-top: 2.5rem;
    margin-bottom: 1rem;
  }

  #panel-history ul {
    margin: 1rem 0 0;
    padding-left: 1.5rem;
  }

  #panel-history li {
    margin: 0.5rem 0;
    line-height: 1.6;
  }

  .timeline-cards {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: repeat(2, minmax(0, 1fr));
    gap: 1.5rem;
    margin: 2rem 0;
  }

  .card {
    background: var(--bg-secondary);
    border: 1px solid var(--border-color);
    border-radius: 10px;
    padding: 1.25rem;
  }

  .card h3 {
    margin-top: 0 !important;
    margin-bottom: 0.6rem;
  }

  .card-intro {
    color: var(--text-secondary);
    font-size: 0.95rem;
    margin: 0;
  }

  .pill-strip {
    display: flex;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
    gap: 0.5rem;
    margin: 0.75rem 0 1rem;
  }

  .pill {
    display: inline-flex;
    align-items: center;
    padding: 0.4rem 0.8rem;
    border: 1px solid var(--color-teal);
    border-radius: 999px;
    background: var(--bg-secondary);
    color: var(--color-teal);
    font-size: 0.88rem;
    line-height: 1.3;
  }

  .pill.secondary {
    border-color: var(--border-color);
    color: var(--text-secondary);
  }

  .strip-note {
    color: var(--text-secondary);
    line-height: 1.6;
    margin: 0.5rem 0 1.5rem;
  }

  .full-record {
    margin: 2.5rem 0 1rem;
    padding: 1rem;
    background: var(--bg-secondary);
    border: 1px solid var(--border-color);
    border-left: 3px solid var(--color-teal);
    border-radius: 6px;
  }

  .full-record a {
    color: var(--color-teal);
  }

  @media (max-width: 860px) {
    .timeline-cards {
      grid-template-columns: 1fr;
    }
  }
</style>
